A. Business-Service Synchronous Request Flow
	I. Transaction Fetch 
		1. Webhook Option
			1. Create a GET endpoint for below webhooks
				i. 	Heartbeat
				ii. TransactionStart
		
		2. Crone Job Option
			1. Create a crone job for every 2 mins to check in:
				i. 	transations awaiting list
				ii. transation status awaiting list
			
	II. Transaction Processing
		1. If we get notified via webhook, or we query via crone job:
		2. Call WR heartbeat 
			i. If NOK, Do Not fetch the transactions
			ii. Otherwise fetch the transactions in the batch
		3. For each transaction:
			i. Check if it exists in the DB:
				a. If it exists, check the final status of the transaction and update transaction_status table with:
					i.   Txn_Status_Final: <finalStatus|DUPLICATE> eg SUCCESS|DUPLICATE
					ii.  Txn_Status_Final_Desc: DUP: Transaction Duplicated. Previous Transaction Status was SUCCESS
					iii. CONTINUE to the next transaction
				
				b. If the transaction does NOT exist:
					i.  Save it the DB with Txn_Status_Initial & Txn_Status_Final as PROCESSING 
					ii. And Txn_Status_Initial_Desc & Txn_Status_Final_Desc Transaction Received. Processing Started
						  a. If saving fails:
						  		i. CONTINUE to the next transaction
								
					ii. Lock transactio after save success
						  a. If Lock fails:
						  		i.   Update DB with Lock_Status: FAILURE
								ii.  Update DB with Lock_Status_Code: <NOT 200>
								iii. update DB with Txn_Status_Final: NOT_PROCESSED
								iv.  update DB with Txn_Status_Final_Desc: LOCK FAILED: Transaction Locking Failed. Transaction Could Not Be Processed Further
								v.   Update DB with World_Remit_Final_Status: LOCK_FAILURE
								vi.  CONTINUE to the next transaction
								
						  b. Otherwise:
						  		i.   Update DB with Lock_Status: SUCCESS
								ii.  Update DB with Lock_Status_Code: 200
								
					iii. Get the heartbeats for Technical-Service and Transaction-Processor-Service
						  a. If heartbeat is NOK:
						  		i. Set WR response with 0036: /transaction/set/acknowledged
									a. If set/acknowledged is SUCCESS:
						  				i.   Update DB Txn_Status_Initial: PENDING_TIMEOUT
										ii.  Update DB Txn_Status_Initial_Desc: HeartBeat Failure: Transaction Marked As PENDING Due To MS Timeout
										iii. Update DB World_Remit_Initial_Status: ACKNOWLEDGED
										iv.  Update DB with World_Remit_Initial_Res_Code: 0036
										v.   Update DB with World_Remit_Ack_Status_Code: 200
										
									b. Else, 
										i.   Update DB Txn_Status_Initial: PENDING_TIMEOUT
										ii.  Update DB Txn_Status_Initial_Desc: Setting Acknowledged Failed. Transaction To Be Processed via Crone Job
										iii. Update DB with World_Remit_Ack_Status_Code: <NOT 200>
										iv.  Update DB Txn_Status_Final_Desc: Setting Acknowledged Failed.

								ii. CONTINUE to the next transaction
								
					iv. Send transaction to Kafka topic
						  a. If Kafka fails:
						  		i. Respond to WR with 0033: /transaction/set/failed
									a. On new thread Update DB
										i.   Update DB Txn_Status_Final: FAILURE
										ii.  Update DB Txn_Status_Final_Desc: Kafka Failure: Transaction Not Sent To Kafka
										iii. Update DB with World_Remit_Final_Status: FAILURE
										iv.  Update DB with World_Remit_Final_Res_Code: 0033
										
								ii. CONTINUE to the next transaction
								
					iv.   CONTINUE to the next transaction
					

B. Business-Service Response Flow
	1. Listen for transactions response from Technical-Service on a Kafka Topic
	2. Check Lock Status.
		i. If SUCCESS set/paid, set/failed, or set/acknowleged	
		ii. Otherwise, set/lock 
			a. if set/lock fails
				i. set transaction as acknowledged
				ii. From another thread, update transaction_status table with the received Txn_Status_Initial & Txn_Status_Final: PENDING_THIRD_PARTY, SUCCESS, Or, FAILURE
			b. otherwise if set/lock succeeds
				i. set transaction as set/paid, set/failed, or set/acknowleged	
				ii. From another thread, update transaction_status table with the received Txn_Status_Initial & Txn_Status_Final: PENDING_THIRD_PARTY, SUCCESS, Or, FAILURE
		
	
